loween  the Festival of someone did you catch  that although Cochran says it  differently than Dr Sam Loomis did in  Halloween 2 he tells us that children  are sacrificed during the Festival of  salad remember how Michael defaced the  chalkboard leading Loomis to believe  that his crimes were part of a tribute  it turns out that cochrane's plan to  eviscerate the minds of American  trick-or-treaters comes from a similar  motivation which makes this the only  through line between Halloween 2 and  Halloween 3. there is another hint about  the true purpose of the silver Shamrock  masks hidden in one small detail at the  motel  foreign  video would be complete without making  fun of the mature relationship between  Dr chalice and Ellie grimbridge I mean  her father just died earlier that week  and she's already trying to get it on  with a mustache man literally more than  twice her age seriously you're going to  investigate your father's murder why did  you even pack that outfit it's so  ridiculous playing an older guy who gets  with younger girls is exactly what Tom  Atkins was born to do I mean have you  seen the fog and I'm not even making  this up but I was looking into this  movie and learned that the scenes in  Santa Maria were filmed at a place  called Lolita California I do love a  good joke and this is the best ever  despite how unintentionally funny this  movie can be at times and believe me it  can be unintentionally funny  foreign  but despite all of that the way the  mystery set up is actually really well  done or at least kind of well done there  are a lot of details that set up the  fact that the factory workers are robots  like the explanation of the hiring  process he brought in every damn one of  them Factory people from the outside  you think you hired me local boy  no way turn me down flat and the  realization that the initial assassins  autopsy only contains machine parts  we've been doing an autopsy on part of  the car it's still hilarious when you  first hear it there's also a little  foreshadowing about the magic element of  cochrane's plan at the motel a woman  named Marge Gutman can be seen reading  Carlos estranadas the Eagles gift from  what I understand this book is about  sorcery although the magic used to  sacrifice The Mask wearing children is  referred to as witchcraft and although  one of the big Halloween three masks is  a witch there isn't an actual witch in  the movie I read somewhere that Tommy  Lee Wallace named it after the Donovan  song Season of the Witch great song but  it is also not in the movie the finale  shows as kids going out to trick or  treat all over the country which by the  way includes some beautiful shots of the  Halloween Sunset chalice rescues what he  thinks is Ellie but actually turns out  to be robo-ellie not sure how or why  Cochrane had the time to make a perfect  replica of her just to screw with old  chalice or why the robo Ellie never  tries to stop him until after he's  destroyed the factory but whatever I'm  in the to this  I gotta say I love this movie's generous  take on how many cities actually  celebrate Halloween anymore I mean I've  lived in La like five years and I've  never once had a kid come to my door to  trick-or-treat on Halloween yeah I was  disappointed to see the lack of  decorations on most houses when I moved  out here after fighting her off he  inexplicably leaves the car behind and  goes to the gas station where the movie  started to try to get the hypnotic  advert taken off the air who goes  trick-or-treating at a gas station  apparently these kids do and they gather  around the TV as Dr chalice begs the  programmer to take the commercial off of  the three channels that it's airing on  wait you never went trick-or-treating at  a gas station do they get out gas or  candy I don't remember this brings us  back to the main theme that I discussed  about Halloween 3. the silver Shamrock  advert is representative of every TV  commercial attempting to corrupt and  brainwash the youth into becoming their  ideal consumer regardless of any harm  that this might be doing to them  physically or psychologically the bugs  and snakes that pour out of the young  copper boy's head are symbolic of what  is going on inside the heads of children  who are exposed to overbearing  advertising from a young age the parents  of these kids do show some concern  saying things like don't sit too close  or turn down the volume but ultimately  the kids are drawn to the flashy colors  and catchy tunes of the broadcast during  the factory tour we learned that silver  Shamrock used to be a toy manufacturer  and eventually switched to hypnotic  masks and television programs in the  1980s when this movie takes place  television was reaching the peak of its  popularity and Cochrane was just  following what the kids were paying  attention to TV shows were the new toys  and silver Shamrock is a stand-in for  any number of malicious private  companies ready to take advantage of  that like most good movies satire  Halloween 3 was ahead of its time I  think it's because it's hard to notice  that stuff when it's still happening all  around you but then when you revisit a  movie a few years later all of the  satirical jokes hit you right on the  head it's kind of funny that 40 years  later stranger things 3 covered the  exact same stuff as Halloween 3. yes and  I'll definitely have to think about  covering that on my channel sometime  soon as well  hint but if the years since 1978 have  taught us anything it's that you can't  kill Michael Myers and even if you could  he just won't stay dead for long the  Halloween Anthology concept was  abandoned after the poor reception of  Halloween 3 and in 1988 the prolific  slasher would wake up and set his sights  on a new Target which means we've got  more things you missed to discuss in  Halloween form the return of Michael  Myers meanwhile there is a new Halloween  movie Halloween kills just one week away